ction><section class="trust-strip"><div class="container trust-inner"><p>More content is not the goal. <strong>The right content, published consistently,</strong> becomes an asset.</p><div class="trust-points"><span>No copy-paste</span><span>No duplicate posts</span><span>No silent failures</span></div></div></section><section class="section problem-section"><div class="container narrow"><span class="section-label">The problem we solve</span><h2>Content publishing should not restart from zero every week.</h2><p class="lead">Most automated blogging workflows break in the same three places. Content Bridge was designed around removing all three.</p><div class="problem-grid"><article><span>01</span><h3>Half-finished articles</h3><p>The article publishes, but its featured image, meta description and focus keyword remain empty. Someone must open the dashboard and finish it—so nobody does.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Duplicate content</h3><p>A retry publishes the same article twice. Two URLs now compete for one keyword, and neither becomes the clear result.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Silent failure</h3><p>Something breaks, the script still reports success, and three weeks later you discover that nothing was published.</p></article></div></div></section><section class="section process-section" id="process"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading split-heading"><div><span class="section-label">Our process</span><h2>Before the first article, we build the system.</h2></div><p>Automation is the final step, not the whole product. Discovery, research and editorial judgement are what make automated content worth publishing.</p></div><div class="process-list"><article class="process-item"><span class="process-number">01</span><div><h3>Audit and discovery</h3><p>We crawl the site, map existing content, review competitors and surface technical constraints.</p></div><span class="process-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></article><article class="process-item"><span class="process-number">02</span><div><h3>Keyword strategy</h3><p>Search demand, intent and SERP overlap become a keyword universe your business can realistically own.</p></div><span class="process-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></article><article class="process-item"><span class="process-number">03</span><div><h3>Editorial system</h3><p>Every article gets a date, target query, structure, internal links, evidence and a clear next action.</p></div><span class="process-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></article><article class="process-item automation"><span class="process-number">04</span><div><h3>Connect and publish</h3><p>Content Bridge connects to WordPress and executes the approved plan on a controlled schedule.</p></div><span class="process-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></article></div></div></section><section class="section responsibility-section"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading split-heading"><div><span class="section-label">The real division of labour</span><h2>The agent writes the draft. Everything that makes it work is ours.</h2></div><p>Before automation is connected, roughly a month goes into understanding the site, mapping demand and building the plan the agent must follow.</p></div><div class="labour-table-wrap"><table class="labour-table"><thead><tr><th>Content Bridge team</th><th>Content agent</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Audit, keyword research and strategy</td><td>Drafting the article</td></tr><tr><td>The six-month plan and every brief</td><td>Following the brief</td></tr><tr><td>The facts file and permitted claims</td><td>Staying inside those facts</td></tr><tr><td>Author assignment and voice</td><td>Writing in that voice</td></tr><tr><td>Cadence and priority decisions</td><td>Publishing on schedule</td></tr><tr><td>Reading algorithm updates</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td>Monthly review and course correction</td><td>—</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="labour-note">The agent is a very fast writer with perfect memory of your rules. Strategy, judgement and course correction remain human.</p></div></section><section class="section agent-section"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading centered"><span class="section-label">Disciplined execution</span><h2>The agent does more than produce words; it follows the operating rules.</h2><p>The strategy and brief come from our team. The execution layer has clear rules for facts, voice, variation, linking and permissions.</p></div><div class="agent-grid"><article class="agent-card"><span>01</span><h3>Checks the moment, not just the calendar</h3><p>It follows the plan, but can cover a genuinely relevant breaking topic first and return to the calendar afterwards.</p></article><article class="agent-card"><span>02</span><h3>Refuses to invent facts</h3><p>Every number must come from your approved facts file. Without a verified figure, it writes qualitatively instead.</p></article><article class="agent-card"><span>03</span><h3>Writes in a real person&#x27;s voice</h3><p>The author is selected by subject and genuine project experience shapes the voice and closing perspective.</p></article><article class="agent-card"><span>04</span><h3>Varies its rhythm</h3><p>Sentence length, paragraph openings and closing register change deliberately so the output does not read like a template.</p></article><article class="agent-card"><span>05</span><h3>Links internally with intent</h3><p>Service pages and related articles are linked from inside useful sentences—not dumped into an unrelated block.</p></article><article class="agent-card"><span>06</span><h3>Knows what it may not touch</h3><p>The agent drafts; deterministic, reportable scripts control publishing, archiving and calendar updates.</p></article></div></div></section><section class="section features-section" id="features"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading centered"><span class="section-label">The details that matter</span><h2>All the small content tasks your team no longer has to carry.</h2><p>From choosing the topic to confirming publication, every step is defined, visible and adapted to your WordPress site.</p></div><div class="feature-grid"><article class="feature-card"><span class="feature-icon">SEO</span><h3>Every SEO field filled</h3><p>SEO title, meta description, focus keyword, cover image, alt text, canonical and schema arrive complete.</p></article><article class="feature-card"><span class="feature-icon">TAG</span><h3>Intent-aware taxonomy</h3><p>The system understands topic and search intent, then assigns the right categories and tags without taxonomy sprawl.</p></article><article class="feature-card"><span class="feature-icon">1×</span><h3>Publish once, ever</h3><p>Every article has an external ID. Re-running a workflow updates the post instead of creating a competing duplicate.</p></article><article class="feature-card"><span class="feature-icon">LINK</span><h3>Purposeful internal links</h3><p>Articles connect to relevant service pages and earlier content so authority compounds around commercial topics.</p></article><article class="feature-card"><span class="feature-icon">TIME</span><h3>Controlled publishing cadence</h3><p>Publishing speed follows the site&#x27;s authority and crawl capacity—never a burst of low-value AI pages.</p></article><article class="feature-card"><span class="feature-icon">LOG</span><h3>Loud failures, clear reports</h3><p>Every run states what was written, updated, skipped or stopped. Nothing silently disappears from the calendar.</p></article></div><div class="promise-card"><div class="promise-mark" aria-hidden="true">“</div><div><span class="section-label">Clarity from day one</span><h3>See the content roadmap and monthly deliverables before work begins.</h3></div><p>Topics, publishing dates, content status and delivery reports stay visible—so your team always knows what is happening, why it matters and what comes next.</p></div><div class="custom-site-card"><div class="custom-site-code" aria-hidden="true"><span>&lt;/&gt;</span><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><div class="custom-site-copy"><span class="section-label">Not running WordPress?</span><h3>Custom-coded websites get a purpose-built script and integration setup.</h3><p>We review your architecture, APIs, authentication, database and content model, then develop and test publishing logic around your actual infrastructure.</p><div class="custom-site-tags"><span>Custom connector script</span><span>API and field mapping</span><span>Publishing and duplicate controls</span><span>Server-level testing</span></div></div><a class="custom-site-link" href="#contact">Technical discovery <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></div></section><section class="section plugin-download-section" id="download-plugin"><div class="container"><div class="plugin-download-card"><div class="plugin-download-icon" aria-hidden="true"><span>CB</span><small>WP</small></div><div class="plugin-download-copy"><span class="section-label">Official WordPress plugin</span><h2>Connect your site to a secure content publishing pipeline.</h2><p>Version 2.1.0 receives articles, featured images, taxonomy, complete SEO fields and FAQ data through a secure endpoint, while duplicate-safe updates keep every article unique.</p><div class="plugin-download-tags"><span>Secure REST API</span><span>Duplicate protection</span><span>Yoast and Rank Math</span><span>Logs and diagnostics</span></div></div><div class="plugin-download-action"><span class="plugin-version">Version 2.1.0</span><a class="button plugin-download-button" href="../downloads/content-bridge-2.1.0.zip" download="">Download plugin <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><small>WordPress 5.6+ · PHP 7.4+</small></div></div></div></section><section class="section seo-proof-section" id="seo-proof"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading split-heading seo-proof-heading"><div><span class="section-label">SEO informed by current data</span><h2>Built for search in 2026—not an outdated SEO checklist.</h2></div><p>The March 2026 core update ran from March 27 to April 8. SE Ranking data showed substantially more movement than the December update.</p></div><div class="seo-stat-grid"><article><strong>79.5%</strong><span>of top-three URLs changed position</span></article><article><strong>24.1%</strong><span>of top-10 pages dropped beyond the top 100</span></article><article><strong>12 days</strong><span>and four hours of official rollout time</span></article></div><div class="seo-response-grid"><div><h3>How the pipeline responds</h3><p>Every article must contain something an aggregator cannot restate: first-hand experience, identifiable authorship, approved facts and a direct connection to your services.</p></div><ul><li><span>Destination source</span><b>Your projects, decisions and observations</b></li><li><span>Identifiable authorship</span><b>A real name with subject relevance</b></li><li><span>Defensible claims</span><b>Every figure comes from an approved facts file</b></li><li><span>Extractable structure</span><b>Direct answers, FAQ, schema and purposeful links</b></li></ul></div><div class="source-links"><span>Sources:</span><a href="https://status.search.google.com/products/rGHU1u87FJnkP6W2GwMi/history?success=true" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Google Search Status</a><a href="https://searchengineland.com/march-2026-google-core-update-what-changed-474397" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">SE Ranking via Search Engine Land</a></div></div></section><section class="section roadmap-section"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading centered"><span class="section-label">The first six months</span><h2>Each month adds a measurable layer to the system.</h2><p>The calendar is not a rigid contract. It follows the site&#x27;s real data and is rebuilt for the next stage at the end of the cycle.</p></div><div class="roadmap-list"><article class="roadmap-item"><span class="roadmap-dot">1</span><div><small>Month 1</small><h3>Foundation</h3><p>The connection and full test are complete, the calendar starts running and publishing no longer depends on manual reminders.</p></div></article><article class="roadmap-item"><span class="roadmap-dot">2</span><div><small>Month 2</small><h3>Indexation and first signals</h3><p>Pages enter the index and Search Console begins surfacing long-tail and question-shaped queries.</p></div></article><article class="roadmap-item"><span class="roadmap-dot">3</span><div><small>Month 3</small><h3>Topical shape</h3><p>Internal links gather articles around core services, turning isolated pages into visible topic clusters.</p></div></article><article class="roadmap-item"><span class="roadmap-dot">4</span><div><small>Months 4–5</small><h3>Compounding</h3><p>Older content produces data, service pages benefit from purposeful links and the next month&#x27;s direction becomes more precise.</p></div></article><article class="roadmap-item"><span class="roadmap-dot">5</span><div><small>Month 6</small><h3>Data-led reassessment</h3><p>The strongest clusters, useful questions and new opportunities are clear enough to rebuild the next calendar.</p></div></article></div></div></section><section class="section guardrails-section"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading split-heading"><div><span class="section-label">Guardrails by design</span><h2>The constraints are part of the product.</h2></div><p>Good automation knows more than what to do. It knows when to stop, verify or return a decision to a person.</p></div><div class="guardrail-grid"><article class="guardrail-card"><span aria-hidden="true">✓</span><div><h3>A cadence for your site</h3><p>Publishing limits come from authority, competition, existing content and crawl speed.</p></div></article><article class="guardrail-card"><span aria-hidden="true">✓</span><div><h3>No fabricated numbers</h3><p>The agent may only use claims and figures from your approved facts file.</p></div></article><article class="guardrail-card"><span aria-hidden="true">✓</span><div><h3>No thin overlap</h3><p>A topic that substantially overlaps existing content changes angle or leaves the calendar.</p></div></article><article class="guardrail-card"><span aria-hidden="true">✓</span><div><h3>Draft by default</h3><p>Direct publishing remains off until you explicitly enable it.</p></div></article><article class="guardrail-card"><span aria-hidden="true">✓</span><div><h3>Fail closed</h3><p>If existing content cannot be checked, the run stops instead of risking a duplicate.</p></div></article></div></div></section><section class="section pricing-section" id="pricing"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading centered pricing-heading"><span class="section-label">Plans</span><h2>Every plan includes the complete strategy.</h2><p>Audit, keyword research and a six-month calendar are complete in every plan. The difference is the final delivery—not the strategic depth.</p></div><div class="pricing-grid"><article class="price-card"><span class="plan-eyebrow">A professional start</span><h3>Base</h3><div class="price"><strong>9</strong><span>million Toman<br/>per month</span></div><p class="plan-description">For businesses that want a consistently published blog built on sound strategy and complete SEO.</p><ul><li><span aria-hidden="true">✓</span>Complete structural, content and technical site audit</li><li><span aria-hidden="true">✓</span>Competitor review and content-gap analysis</li><li><span aria-hidden="true">✓</span>Keyword research and SERP-overlap clustering</li><li><span aria-hidden="true">✓</span>Search-intent analysis and article-format selection</li><li><span aria-hidden="true">✓</span>Dated six-month editorial calendar</li><li><span aria-hidden="true">✓</span>A dedicated brief for every article</li><li><span aria-hidden="true">✓</span>Plugin installation and site configuration</li><li><span aria-hidden="true">✓</span>Hosting and server compatibility fixes</li><li><span aria-hidden="true">✓</span>Automated, scheduled W